# netsurf: bitmaps and the disc/arc/path ops paint at the composed group opacity (patch 315)
# Generated 2026-10-25
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 314)
#
# Doc 24 stage 1 (the bitmap opacity channel). Patch 314 recorded the
# remainder of patch 311's gap: at partial group opacity, fills, text
# and borders faded but images, radio buttons and inline SVG painted
# solid. The bitmap plot op had no opacity channel, and the disc, arc
# and path ops ignored the opacity their plot style could carry.
#
#  - include/netsurf/plotters.h: BITMAPF_OPACITY(a), a byte in flag bits
#    16-23 beside the blend-mode encoding (doc 24 shape (a)). A masked 0
#    means "not supplied" = opaque, which is what every caller that never
#    writes the field produces; folding sites write >= 1 for a real value.
#    It rides in the op, so desktop knockout's queued replay keeps it.
#  - Correction to doc 24's census: background images do NOT reach the
#    plotter from redraw.c directly -- html_redraw_background and the
#    inline-background path paint through content_redraw() and the image
#    handler. So the carrier doc 24 scheduled for stage 2 is needed here:
#    content_redraw_data gains `opacity` (a byte, 0 = solid). redraw.c
#    fills it at both background sites from the new
#    html_redraw_group_opacity_byte() (the patch-314 composed value,
#    rounded, 0 when full so solid pages' flags are unchanged), and the
#    four handlers that call the bitmap op (image.c -- png/jpeg/gif/ico/
#    webp via image_bitmap_plot -- bmp.c, nssprite.c, rsvg.c) fold
#    BITMAPF_OPACITY(data->opacity) beside their blend fold, so it
#    composes with the REPEAT and blend bits. Every other constructor of
#    the struct (content.c thumbnails, browser_window.c, print.c,
#    treeview.c, and redraw.c's <img>/object data) sets opacity = 0:
#    <img> at group opacity is doc 24 stage 2 and still paints solid.
#    The two redraw.c sites that call the bitmap op directly fold the
#    byte too: the background-clip:text image and a <canvas>.
#  - frontends/vita/plot.c, bitmap op: bucket from the byte (the same
#    thresholds as every other op). Bucket 0 skips the draw. A tile drawn
#    1:1 (op size == texture size) at a partial bucket draws through
#    vita2d_draw_texture_tint_part with a white tint at the bucket alpha
#    -- the stub-declared entry the text atlas already uses; libvita2d's
#    tint shader multiplies texel by tint. A SCALED tile still draws
#    solid: no stub entry both scales and tints (doc 24's open fork: CPU
#    pre-multiply vs a device-verified scale-tint entry -- the owner's
#    call). The trace appends " OPAQUE <bucket>" only to a draw that is
#    actually faded or skipped, so solid pages' dumps are byte-identical
#    and a declined scaled fade reads as solid.
#  - disc/arc/path: per-op adoption of vita_geom_opacity_bucket(style),
#    exactly as patch 314 did for line/polygon/rectangle -- disc fill and
#    stroke, arc stroke, the path filler's spans and strokes, with the
#    OPAQUE trace suffix only when non-solid. Their callers passed shared
#    static styles (radio) or a zeroed one (inline SVG), so the group
#    opacity is folded in there: html_redraw_radio takes local copies of
#    its four styles, vb_inline_svg_paint sets ps.opacity.
#  - replay.c honours a BITMAP line's OPAQUE suffix like RECT/LINE.
#
# Simulator (tools/vita-sim/vitasim.c, same commit): its tint_part used
# the tint colour as paint with texel alpha as coverage -- right for the
# U8 text atlas, wrong for an RGBA texture (doc 24 assumed texel x tint).
# RGBA textures now modulate every channel by the tint, as the libvita2d
# shader does; the U8 path is unchanged (text pixels identical).
#
# Proof (focused, sim): inside opacity:.5 a 20x20 blue (0,0,255) no-repeat
# tile reads 127,127,255; a 16x16 red tile repeated in both axes with
# background-blend-mode set reads 255,127,127 in its first tile and its
# last row/column; the same repeat outside the group reads 255,0,0 with
# no token. A checked radio inside the group traces 2 DISC + 2 ARC
# OPAQUE 2 (its centre dot 0 -> 117), the control none; an inline SVG
# rect reads 127,127,255 vs 0,0,255 outside. Gate: CSS-opacity-group
# gains the row; the gate script asserts the counts and the four pixels.
#
# Scope notes (recorded, not changed here):
#  - Scaled bitmaps at partial opacity: solid, as above (doc 24 open
#    question 1). <img> and other object contents: stage 2.
#  - image_bitmap_plot's 1x1-bitmap shortcut plots a rectangle with a
#    stack plot_style_t whose opacity/radius/shadow fields are never
#    initialised (pre-existing): a 1x1 background inside a group cannot
#    fade, and those fields are whatever the stack held. Not touched.
#  - SVG image contents (content/handlers/image/svg.c) build their own
#    path styles and do not fold the group opacity; checkbox gadgets
#    (rect/line with static styles) likewise. Same class, next stage.
#
# Simulator only; the vita cross-build was not run for this patch.
# Device expectation is in Doc 10.
